---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { site } from '../../site';
---

<Docs
  title="Car and offline"
  toc={[
    ['auto', 'Android Auto'],
    ['unknown-sources', 'Unknown sources'],
    ['offline', 'The web app offline'],
  ]}
  description={`Browse and play ${site.name} in Android Auto, and start the web app without a connection.`}
>
  <h1>In the car and offline</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    {site.name} plays in Android Auto with the phone in your pocket, and the web app starts without
    a connection once you have opened it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="auto">Android Auto</h2>
  <p>
    In the car, {site.name} shows five shelves: <strong>Continue listening</strong>,
    <strong>On this phone</strong> (local folders and downloads), <strong>Podcasts</strong> (the
    newest unplayed episode of each subscription), <strong>Up Next</strong> and
    <strong>Lists</strong>. Picking a book plays it from its saved place, the same way the app does.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each of your lists opens on <strong>Play list</strong>, which starts where the list stands, then
    its items. A list goes on from item to item by itself, and the player's menu has Previous and
    Next in list.
  </p>
  <p>
    The shelves come from the playback service, so they work when the app is closed. They show what
    the app knew the last time it was open; open the app once to bring them up to date after you add
    books or subscribe to podcasts on another device.
  </p>
  <p>
    Downloaded books and local folders play without a connection. Streamed books and episodes need
    one, just like on the phone.
  </p>

  <h2 id="unknown-sources">Unknown sources</h2>
  <p>
    Android Auto only lists media apps from the Play Store unless you allow others. {site.name} is
    installed from its own APK, so turn this on once:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      On the phone, open Android Auto’s settings (Settings → Connected devices → Android Auto).
    </li>
    <li>
      Tap <strong>Version</strong> at the bottom about ten times until developer settings unlock.
    </li>
    <li>
      Open the menu (⋮) → <strong>Developer settings</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Turn on <strong>Unknown sources</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Disconnect from the car and connect again. {site.name} now appears among the media apps.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The setting only lets Android Auto list apps that were not installed from the Play Store. It
    gives {site.name} no extra permissions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="offline">The web app offline</h2>
  <p>
    The web app keeps its own files (the page, its code, the database engine and icons) in the
    browser, so after the first visit it starts without a connection. Your library lives in the
    browser already; downloaded books play offline as well.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Add-on catalogs and podcast feeds load from the network first. Offline, the app shows the last
      answer it got.
    </li>
    <li>
      Audio is never kept by this cache. Streaming needs a connection; use downloads for offline
      listening.
    </li>
    <li>
      A new version installs in the background and takes over the next time you open the app after
      closing every tab of it.
    </li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
